
  <sn><md>#### Food Chain

The biotic component of the ecosystem i.e., the plants and animals, are interdependent on each other for their nutritional requirement.

For example, Producers form food for the herbivores, which in turn forms the food for carnivores.

&gt; The `transfer of energy and nutrients` from one feeding group of organisms to another `in a series` is called Food chain. It is the sequence of who eats whom.

In nature, basically `two types` of food chains are recognized – **grazing food chain** and **detritus food chain**.
</md></sn>
